  31:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) If needed , configure the reception filters and optional features using
  32:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           the following configuration functions:
  33:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigFilter
  34:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigGlobalFilter
  35:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigExtendedIdMask
  36:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigRxFifoOverwrite
  37:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigRamWatchdog
  38:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigTimestampCounter
  39:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_EnableTimestampCounter
  40:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_DisableTimestampCounter
  41:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigTimeoutCounter
  42:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_EnableTimeoutCounter
  43:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_DisableTimeoutCounter
  44:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_ConfigTxDelayCompensation
  45:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_EnableTxDelayCompensation
  46:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_DisableTxDelayCompensation
  47:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_EnableISOMode
  48:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_DisableISOMode
  49:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_EnableEdgeFiltering
  50:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_DisableEdgeFiltering
  51:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  52:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) Start the FDCAN module using HAL_FDCAN_Start function. At this level
  53:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           the node is active on the bus: it can send and receive messages.
  54:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  55:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) The following Tx control functions can only be called when the FDCAN
  56:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           module is started:
  57:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_AddMessageToTxFifoQ
  58:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_AbortTxRequest
  59:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  60:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) After having submitted a Tx request in Tx Fifo or Queue, it is possible to
  61:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           get Tx buffer location used to place the Tx request thanks to
  62:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           HAL_FDCAN_GetLatestTxFifoQRequestBuffer API.
  63:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           It is then possible to abort later on the corresponding Tx Request using
  64:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           HAL_FDCAN_AbortTxRequest API.
  65:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  66:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) When a message is received into the FDCAN message RAM, it can be
  67:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           retrieved using the HAL_FDCAN_GetRxMessage function.
  68:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  69:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) Calling the HAL_FDCAN_Stop function stops the FDCAN module by entering
  70:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           it to initialization mode and re-enabling access to configuration
  71:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           registers through the configuration functions listed here above.
  72:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  73:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) All other control functions can be called any time after initialization
  74:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           phase, no matter if the FDCAN module is started or stopped.
  75:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  76:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       *** Polling mode operation ***
  77:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       ==============================
  78:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     [..]
  79:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****         (#) Reception and transmission states can be monitored via the following
  80:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             functions:
  81:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****               (++) HAL_FDCAN_IsTxBufferMessagePending
  82:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****               (++) HAL_FDCAN_GetRxFifoFillLevel
  83:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****               (++) HAL_FDCAN_GetTxFifoFreeLevel
  84:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  85:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       *** Interrupt mode operation ***
  86:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       ================================
  87:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       [..]
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc2SU6oB.s 			page 3


  88:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****         (#) There are two interrupt lines: line 0 and 1.
  89:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             By default, all interrupts are assigned to line 0. Interrupt lines
  90:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             can be configured using HAL_FDCAN_ConfigInterruptLines function.
  91:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  92:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****         (#) Notifications are activated using HAL_FDCAN_ActivateNotification
  93:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             function. Then, the process can be controlled through one of the
  94:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             available user callbacks: HAL_FDCAN_xxxCallback.
  95:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  96:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
  97:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   =============================================
  98:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  99:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   The compilation define USE_HAL_FDCAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 100:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 101:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Use Function HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() or HAL_FDCAN_RegisterXXXCallback()
 102:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   to register an interrupt callback.
 103:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 104:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Function HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 105:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TxFifoEmptyCallback          : Tx Fifo Empty Callback.
 106:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) HighPriorityMessageCallback  : High Priority Message Callback.
 107:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimestampWraparoundCallback  : Timestamp Wraparound Callback.
 108:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimeoutOccurredCallback      : Timeout Occurred Callback.
 109:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                : Error Callback.
 110:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback              : FDCAN MspInit.
 111:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback            : FDCAN MspDeInit.
 112:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 113:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and a pointer to the user callback function.
 114:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 115:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   For specific callbacks TxEventFifoCallback, RxFifo0Callback, RxFifo1Callback,
 116:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   TxBufferCompleteCallback, TxBufferAbortCallback and ErrorStatusCallback use dedicated
 117:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   register callbacks: respectively HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxEventFifoCallback(),
 118:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_RegisterRxFifo0Callback(), HAL_FDCAN_RegisterRxFifo1Callback(),
 119:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxBufferCompleteCallback(), HAL_FDCAN_RegisterTxBufferAbortCallback()
 120:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and HAL_FDCAN_RegisterErrorStatusCallback().
 121:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 122:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Use function HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 123:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   weak function.
 124:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 125:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and the Callback ID.
 126:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 127:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TxFifoEmptyCallback          : Tx Fifo Empty Callback.
 128:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) HighPriorityMessageCallback  : High Priority Message Callback.
 129:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimestampWraparoundCallback  : Timestamp Wraparound Callback.
 130:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) TimeoutOccurredCallback      : Timeout Occurred Callback.
 131:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                : Error Callback.
 132:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback              : FDCAN MspInit.
 133:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback            : FDCAN MspDeInit.
 134:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 135:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   For specific callbacks TxEventFifoCallback, RxFifo0Callback, RxFifo1Callback,
 136:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   TxBufferCompleteCallback and TxBufferAbortCallback, use dedicated
 137:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   unregister callbacks: respectively HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxEventFifoCallback(),
 138:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterRxFifo0Callback(), HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterRxFifo1Callback(),
 139:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxBufferCompleteCallback(), HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterTxBufferAbortCallback()
 140:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   and HAL_FDCAN_UnRegisterErrorStatusCallback().
 141:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 142:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   By default, after the HAL_FDCAN_Init() and when the state is HAL_FDCAN_STATE_RESET,
 143:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 144:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   examples HAL_FDCAN_ErrorCallback().
ARM GAS  /tmp/cc2SU6oB.s 			page 4


 145:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 146:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   reset to the legacy weak function in the HAL_FDCAN_Init()/ HAL_FDCAN_DeInit() only when
 147:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 148:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   if not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_FDCAN_Init()/ HAL_FDCAN_DeInit()
 149:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 150:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 151:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_FDCAN_STATE_READY state only.
 152:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 153:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   in HAL_FDCAN_STATE_READY or HAL_FDCAN_STATE_RESET state,
 154:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 155:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 156:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   using HAL_FDCAN_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_FDCAN_DeInit()
 157:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   or HAL_FDCAN_Init() function.
 158:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 159:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   When The compilation define USE_HAL_FDCAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 160:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 161:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 162:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
 163:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   @endverbatim
 164:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****   ******************************************************************************
